<h3>A.1 &nbsp;Recorded numerical checks</h3>
<p>The Limite TileLang prototype qualification compares against independent FP32 attention oracles. For the recorded local context-2,048/span-1,025 case, output relative L2 error is 0.00043244 and the largest input-gradient relative L2 error is 0.00450935. For the global context-2,048 case, the corresponding values are 0.00041044 and 0.00407004. The declared bounds are 0.005 for output and 0.01 for input gradients; these are norm-ratio bounds, not elementwise relative tolerances. Separate fresh-adapter admissions record zero initial output error, matching frozen-parent hashes, finite three-step updates, and exact checkpoint restoration. These are historical qualification observations, not new GPU tests performed for this paper.</p>
<h3>A.2 &nbsp;Identity, exclusions, and availability</h3>
<p>The AIME source snapshot is <code>MathArena/aime_2026@d2de22f3c656b4f56cf8981212186377d1e23bc3</code>. The historical strict grader uses <code>math-verify 0.8.0</code>; the current dependency declaration is not a substitute for the historical environment. Template/tokenizer lineage is recorded against Violetto revision <code>4cf321846e479e78d9ec35dbd39fee2e260cbad6</code>. The compact Limite endpoint record refers to historical source <code>dfb0ab4622bf6c30f3d09612328eb43827f8a067</code>. These identities do not imply that the public snapshot contains their full history.</p>
<p>The incomplete 8B AIME evaluation is excluded. The original random-feature sampler used incorrect radial and QR-sign handling and is excluded as evidence for its intended operator. The later triadic scratch attempts do not supply a post-training held-out comparison and are not pooled with exact-simplicial results. No checkpoints, raw reasoning traces, private service endpoints, or live job state are packaged with this manuscript.</p>
